    add('The fixed cohort contains 4,096 IID truth/source draws with no pilot outcomes or continuation-frequency requirement. For zero, one and two extra D4 leaper orbits, the declared prior assigns P(k)=1/3 and distributes that mass uniformly over C(55,k) models. After conditioning on M≥8, there are 1,522 eligible models: 1, 55 and 1,466 respectively. Their exact integer weights are 1,485, 27 and 1, totaling 4,436. The 19 ineligible models remain in the full catalog and frequency table with zero conditional mass.');add()
    add('Case `i` draws an integer ticket using `default_rng(2026700000+i).integers(4436)` and maps it through candidate-ID-ordered half-open cumulative intervals. An independent stream `default_rng(2026800000+i).choice(M,8,replace=False)` supplies eight distinct positives. No floating-point probabilities, rejection, resampling or outcome-dependent selection are used. All truth/source draws are logged before any new target label. Prefreeze checks enumerate all 4,436 tickets, independently recount every source cardinality from packed masks, and verify candidate/orbit/cardinality identity against the original catalog. All 8,192 new truth/source seeds are distinct and avoid explicitly recorded historical seed values.');add()
    add('| Added orbit count | Eligible models | Prior integer mass | Expected draws from fixed sampling law | Observed draws | Distinct sampled models | Exact cases | First-lex / posterior / uniform continuation |');add('|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|')
    for k in [0,1,2]:
        rows=[r for r in s['truth_results'] if len(p['truths'][r['candidate']]['orbits'])==k];eligible=sum(r['eligible'] for r in rows);mass=sum(r['prior_integer_weight'] for r in rows);costs=[sum(r['continuation_calls'][mode] for r in rows) for mode in ['firstlex','posterior','uniform']];add(f"| {k} | {eligible:,} | {mass:,} | {4096*mass/4436:.6f} | {sum(r['cases'] for r in rows):,} | {sum(r['cases']>0 for r in rows):,} | {sum(r['exact_cases'] for r in rows):,} | {' / '.join(map(str,costs))} |")
    add();add('Expected class counts above follow the exact sampling law; observed class/cost breakdowns are descriptive. All 1,541 candidate rows are retained in [the full truth table](../../../../results/research/loki/h3br/truth-costs.csv), including unobserved eligible models and all ineligible models. The cohort sampled 909 distinct truth models, so it is not an exhaustive trial of every eligible model.');add()
    add(f"All {s['cases']:,} cases remain in scope. The {s['prior_success_cases']:,} MAP-stage successes use no continuation queries. The {s['feasible_checkpoint_cases']} feasible checkpoints map to {s['distinct_feasible_sets']} distinct sets; {s['infeasible_checkpoint_cases']} infeasible checkpoints remain unresolved. There are {s['distinct_compiled_sets']} unresolved candidate sets in total. All policies produce the same per-case exact flag and identify {s['exact_cases']:,} cases. Equality is a required correctness invariant, not another empirical success criterion.");add()
    add('The unchanged source score is C(55,k) C(M,8). Conditioning the truth prior on M≥8 introduces only a common normalization factor, while eight distinct positives already exclude models with M<8. All other compatible models, including M from eight through fifteen, remain candidates. Deterministic MAP query answers filter the candidate set without changing relative posterior weights among survivors. The shared selector uses at most four queries, exact score/ID guide ties and lexicographic maximum-disagreement board ties.');add()
    add('All shared MAP checkpoints are completed before compilation. First-lex trees use the unchanged feasibility compiler; posterior and uniform trees use the byte-identical exact weighted optimizer with reciprocal-score integer weights or all-one weights. The full N13 query universe contains 73,712 ordinary boards. Every candidate set, weight vector, depth, catalog hash, prediction hash and compiler hash is bound in the cache identity. Compilers receive no case or true identity. All three policies for all sets are bound before any continuation label.');add()
    add('For every feasible set, the posterior-weighted objective of its optimal tree is checked to be no larger than that of the uniform-optimal tree. This is a pointwise optimization property. Under the matched sampling model, expected nonincrease follows from the stated posterior; a realized 2% saving in this finite cohort does not follow automatically and remains the scientific endpoint. If the uniform comparator had zero continuation calls, the primary would have been inconclusive. Exact infeasibility certificates are shared across the common depth-four class; missing/capped/unexpectedly infeasible optimized proofs make the entire study incomplete, with no fallback or partial claim.');add()
    add(f"The study newly charges **{s['actual_membership_calls']:,} membership calls**: {s['shared_MAP_calls']:,} shared MAP plus {F:,} first-lex, {P:,} posterior and {U:,} uniform continuations. Summing the three policy totals would count shared MAP three times. Each query is flushed and fsynced before its separate oracle read and immediate hash-linked answer. All {s['cross_policy_reacquisitions']} cross-policy same-case query reacquisitions are paid; no cached or archived answer replaces an invocation. There are {s['unique_same_case_query_boards']:,} distinct case/query-board pairs.");add()
    add(f"The {s['source_positive_union_appearances']:,} positive source appearances are shared across three arms ({s['positive_arm_appearances']:,} arm appearances), with {s['distinct_N12_boards']:,} distinct N12 boards globally. All {s['source_cases_with_prior_same_study_duplicates']} cases repeating a previously drawn unordered source bank remain included. There are {s['source_cases_matching_archived_eight_banks']} exact bank matches against H3bm/H3bq eight-positive banks; individual-board overlap is allowed. These bookkeeping counts do not alter the cohort.");add()
